"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fd5d4fe8c80897e6bbc8da10e2b2455456fcf38806fc686c3a3231ba395074d4","event_uuid":"6a434701-5f21-49d3-9e23-1de8a0c4af83","position":{"commit_sha":"027b673815a3bfba16c5f9f421ca47e7c3dd5aeb","position":"1788573544064928754-6a434701-5f21-49d3-9e23-1de8a0c4af83"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788469697004204527,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bc521c16-64ab-44ac-807b-c49c17f9a2a2","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"afe3-5aec-51cb-4e02"},{"link_uuid":"2b3a8d3d-c515-4996-a7cd-029e6a333345","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3952-0886-0419-4736"},{"link_uuid":"7cb9ccfa-363c-4891-b8dc-67754d8ffce3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8086-0cb9-8fed-4a99"},{"link_uuid":"6a434701-5f21-49d3-9e23-1de8a0c4af83","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d029-a02c-7ca0-4cd0"}],"description":"## Context\n\nBoth review pipelines already have Terraform-scoped tool sessions [rebar:salmon-abominable-pupa]. This slice adds `probe_source` to disprove a claim that a declared module/provider source is unavailable when it is local or its registry metadata is positively reachable. It never downloads module content and never treats failed access as nonexistence — positive-only, like Rebar's package-existence oracle: reachable evidence refutes; inaccessible says nothing.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_source.py` and a `probe_source` method on the `terraform_tools.py` session, then mint it as the THIRD Terraform tool at the single shared site `plan_review/terraform_seam.py` (`_session_tools`/`build_tool_provider`) — which serves BOTH pipelines (code-review's `code_review/terraform_grounding.py` delegates to `build_tool_provider`), so plan-review and code-review IaC Pass-1/Pass-2 all advertise it.\n\n### Local sources\n\n- Normalize literal local source forms relative to `from_module`; return positive T1 only when the resolved dir stays under the repo root, holds an indexable module, and is in the bounded immutable closure.\n- An absolute path, escaping `../`, escaping symlink, unreadable dir, missing target, or dynamic source returns ABSTAIN (absence never asserted). `.terraform/modules` is excluded (generated, may be stale, not attested).\n\n### Registry metadata\n\n- Recognize provider and native module registry addresses (incl. explicit hostnames); normalize omitted hostnames to the default. Use Registry service discovery and version/metadata endpoints only, never a download URL. Accept positive T0 evidence only after a bounded HTTPS response is successful, size-limited, and schema-valid.\n- Permit the public default registry; for a custom host, permit a globally routable DNS target or an exact hostname trusted by an ambient credential entry. Reject embedded URL credentials, literal IPs, non-HTTPS, and cross-host redirects; a private-address host needs the exact credentialed hostname.\n- Bound metadata to 1 MiB/response and the 60-second deadline; reuse the grounding fail-open worker/harness and stdlib `urllib` (no new dependency). `deps.py:_http_get` returns only a status int, so `probe_source` adds a bounded HTTPS helper (same monkeypatchable seam) returning status, final URL, and a size-capped body. Redirect-following is DISABLED (no-redirect opener): a cross-host redirect is `network_error` before any credential attaches; the token attaches only after target validation.\n- A 2xx schema-valid response yields only a closed `source_kind` (`local_module` | `registry_provider` | `registry_module`) plus the existing `result_digest`, never response bodies, raw counts, or remote source contents.\n\n### Ambient credentials\n\nFollow Terraform's precedence and hostname normalization: (1) `TF_TOKEN_<hostname>` env credential; (2) `TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE` else platform-default CLI config; (3) `credentials.tfrc.json`.\n\nRead only literal `credentials` entries for the exact registry hostname. Never prompt, write a credential file, run a `credentials_helper`, import cloud/provider credentials, or use another host's. Output/receipts/logs identify only `auth_source=environment|static-file|none` — no token, hash, path, header, or raw error body.\n\n### Receipt schema & outcome (closed-enum extension)\n\n`probe_source` uses `job=refute`: a positive registry hit refutes at T0, a positive local module at T1; every other result is ABSTAIN (mapped below), never an “absent”/negative. It rides the same per-call session and closed `terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json`, extending those enums rather than adding a parallel receipt:\n\n- **`operation` enum** (schema + `terraform_receipt.py`) gains `probe_source` beside `lookup_declaration`/`resolve_reference`.\n- **`source_kind`** is an OPTIONAL closed-enum property on the receipt's top-level `properties` (`additionalProperties:false` stays; NOT in `required`, so existing `lookup_declaration`/`resolve_reference` receipts that omit it still validate). It appears only on a `probe_source` `refuted` receipt and lives on the RECEIPT, not the evidence record (generic `grounding.schema.json` unchanged). Positive metadata rides `source_kind` + existing `result_digest`; no raw counts/bodies become new fields.\n- **Probe query shape** `{operation:\"probe_source\", source, from_module}`, redacted identically — no token, header, home path, or resolved absolute path in the hashed query. Positive outcomes reuse the existing refuted evidence/receipt path (`provenance_tier` T0/T1).\n- **`reason_detail` enum + `ABSTENTIONS` table** gain closed probe keys, each mapped to an existing generic `reason` in `evidence.ABSTAIN_REASONS`: `registry_not_found`/`registry_unauthorized`→`private_or_internal_suspected`; `registry_rate_limited`→`rate_limited`; `dns_error`/`tls_error`/`proxy_error`/`registry_server_error`/`rejected_redirect`→`network_error`; `probe_timeout`→`timeout`; `malformed_metadata`/`oversized_metadata`→`parse_error`; `rejected_target`/`non_registry_remote`/`dynamic_source`→`ambiguous`.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRemote module downloads/fetch, Git/HTTP/S3/GCS checkout, Terraform Cloud API beyond registry discovery, credential helpers, new auth config, provider/cloud credentials, and all Terraform/OpenTofu/provider execution. The ADR records ambient-credential remote fetch as approved-but-deferred (not in V1).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Local-source tests return positive T1 for a repo-contained child and ABSTAIN for missing, absolute, escaping, symlink-escaping, unreadable, generated-cache, and dynamic sources, exposing no partial facts.\n- [ ] Registry protocol tests return positive T0 evidence only for schema-valid provider/module metadata and assert no download URL/archive endpoint is requested; receipt `operation` is `probe_source` with a closed `source_kind`.\n- [ ] The closed receipt schema is extended, not bypassed: schema + `terraform_receipt.py` accept `operation=\"probe_source\"` and every probe `reason_detail` key mapped to an existing generic `reason`; a schema test rejects an unknown `reason_detail` and `operation`.\n- [ ] Credential-precedence tests cover hostname encoding, env-over-static precedence, `TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE`, platform defaults, and `credentials.tfrc.json`; helper blocks ignored; no credential value/hash/path appears in results, receipts, logs, or diagnostics.\n- [ ] The access matrix maps 401/403/404, 429, DNS, TLS, proxy, 5xx, rejected redirect, timeout, malformed JSON, and oversized response to the specified closed abstention, never nonexistence.\n- [ ] Network-target tests allow the public default registry, a globally routable custom registry, and an exact credentialed private hostname, rejecting HTTP, embedded credentials, literal IPs, uncredentialed private targets, and cross-host redirects before any token is sent.\n- [ ] Plan-review T10 and code-review IaC Pass 1/2 advertise `probe_source` beside the two existing operations; non-Terraform steps and missing-extra runs advertise none.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0115-terraform-structural-grounding.md` and `docs/grounding.md` distinguish V1 metadata probing from prohibited remote fetch and record ambient-credential fetch as approved-but-deferred.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card — Contract: REB-640 + Terraform's registry/CLI-credential protocols + the tool-session contract [rebar:salmon-abominable-pupa]. Preconditions: temp-repo local modules + a stateful registry fake (valid/auth-required/error/redirect/oversized/download-advertising). Production path: real normalization/credential-selection/response-parsing through the tool, only DNS/socket faked. Oracles: exact outcome/tier/reason + endpoint/headers; byte scans prove the secret and download URL never escape. CI: `make test`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_source.py","reason":"new module: normalize local sources, registry addresses, ambient credentials, and positive-only metadata probes"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_tools.py","reason":"add probe_source method to the Terraform-scoped per-call session"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_receipt.py","reason":"extend ABSTENTIONS table and operation handling for probe_source detail keys"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json","reason":"extend closed operation and reason_detail enums for probe_source"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/terraform_seam.py","reason":"mint terraform_probe_source as the third session tool (shared by both pipelines)"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py","reason":"path containment, credential precedence, registry protocol, redaction, and abstention contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py","reason":"plan-review Pass-1 and Pass-2 probe_source routing"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py","reason":"code-review IaC Pass-1 and Pass-2 probe_source routing"},{"path":"docs/adr/0115-terraform-structural-grounding.md","reason":"record source trust boundary and approved-but-deferred ambient remote fetch"},{"path":"docs/grounding.md","reason":"document local and registry source probing, credentials, limits, and access-error abstention"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/grounding.schema.json","reason":"add 'source' to the reference kind enum: probe_source emits reference={kind:source} receipts"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated registry (gen_env_registry.py staleness gate): TF_CLI_CONFIG_FILE + dynamic TF_TOKEN_* read from terraform_source.py"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","afe3-5aec-51cb-4e02"],["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"],["relates_to","3952-0886-0419-4736"],["relates_to","8086-0cb9-8fed-4a99"],["relates_to","d029-a02c-7ca0-4cd0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","parent_status_uuid":"3f8154db-f44f-42b7-b6c5-7df213a9ae99","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["terraform","grounding","registry","credentials","optional"],"ticket_id":"1c52-5e73-4d61-4124","ticket_type":"task","title":"Probe local and registry Terraform sources with ambient access","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py -k local_source","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"repo-contained local hit and every path-containment abstention"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py -k registry","dd_id":"AC2,AC4,AC5","dd_text":"positive-only registry protocol, target policy, no-download assertion, and access-error matrix"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py -k credentials","dd_id":"AC3","dd_text":"Terraform credential precedence plus byte-level secret and path redaction"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py -k probe_source","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"Terraform-only Pass-1/Pass-2 visibility and missing-extra negative controls"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_source.py && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make docs-check","dd_id":"AC7","dd_text":"source-probe contract and approved-but-deferred remote-fetch documentation"}]},"source_event_uuids":["b9a6f329-0945-4515-90d5-611f69815e58","cb92e005-53ba-420c-872f-c00569311191","29be129f-db1d-4dc7-bde7-5dccc22304f6","f65ef6b1-81d4-48bd-a169-63bd238679e8","f3969db3-ad08-46f5-96ca-9cadc7a053af","04a962da-0d20-4b32-ab23-8e92e51ba785","c7cc93be-7fa7-4530-9adb-301113a70c4d","3f8154db-f44f-42b7-b6c5-7df213a9ae99","889a5f1c-c1b4-4108-a6da-d99f875ac2b5","cb9e13dc-39fe-46c9-b066-c233932bd3a8","2b3a8d3d-c515-4996-a7cd-029e6a333345","7cb9ccfa-363c-4891-b8dc-67754d8ffce3","6a434701-5f21-49d3-9e23-1de8a0c4af83"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc968